      "answer": "$45/73=0.616$",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "$4/(x+10)=1/6$, so $x+10=24$ and $x=14$. B1: find $x$; may be implied by correct probabilities. $P(A_R\\mid B_R)=P(A_R\\cap B_R)/P(B_R)=[(6/10)((x+1)/(x+10))]/[(6/10)((x+1)/(x+10))+(4/10)(x/(x+10))]$. B1 FT: $(6/10)((x+1)/(x+10))$ as numerator or denominator. M1: denominator sum with both branches seen anywhere. A1 FT: seen as denominator of fraction. With $x=14$, numerator $=3/8$ and denominator $=73/120$, giving $45/73=0.616[4\\ldots]$. A1. If B0 M0: SC B1 for $3/8$ over $73/120$, or $0.375/0.6083$; SC B1 for $45/73$ or 0.616. Total: 5.",
